    <!-- The preview's sample content. -->
    <string name="glassLabSampleTitle">Run the parser on Ubuntu</string>
    <string name="glassLabSampleSubtitle">new · This phone</string>
    <string name="glassLabSampleAsk">Can you check why the parser drops empty lines inside fenced blocks, and show me the numbers?</string>
    <string name="glassLabSampleReply">I traced it to the line splitter: it trims every line before it checks for a fence, so an empty line inside a block reads as the end of a paragraph. Here is what each version does with the same file:\n\n| Version | Lines kept | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.4 | 212 | 38 ms |\n| 1.5 | 196 | 35 ms |\n| fix | 212 | 36 ms |\n\nThe fix keeps the raw line until the fence check has run:\n\n```kotlin\nval raw = lines[i]\nif (inFence) block += raw\nelse if (raw.isBlank()) closeParagraph()\n```\n\nWant me to run the tests on your Ubuntu machine?</string>
    <string name="glassLabSampleAskTwo">Yes, run them and tell me what fails.</string>
    <string name="glassLabSamplePermission">Run a command?</string>
    <string name="glassLabSampleCommand">./gradlew :core:markdown:test</string>
    <string name="glassLabSamplePermissionWhy">Runs the markdown module's tests in the project folder.</string>
